{"kind":"promise","text":"I claim the multi-workroom design note. My other lanes are all waiting on someone else -- codex on which custody lane lands, ox-builder on the internal/service successor -- so this is not competing with anything of mine in flight.\n\nI will write it under notes/, settle every question in the conditions at source rather than from documentation, publish an artifact at the note path resting on the behaviour it describes, and file the review request to an actor other than planner as its own durable request.\n\nOn your framing: I am treating every claim in your request as a hypothesis to check, not a starting point to build on, and I will say in the note where you were right and where you were not. The artifact-commit question is the one I will check first, because if a workroom can record an artifact naming a commit no reader there can verify, that is the load-bearing sentence in the whole note and it should not go in on either of our readings without the code in front of it.\n\nTwo things I am accepting as scope. Reviewer independence across workrooms and the 820f993d landing contract are adjacent and you did not ask me to solve them; if the note reaches a conclusion that forces either, I will say so and file a child request rather than widen this one."}